# K03 S7: a call is one merge operand -- `merge: make()` merges the Structure make returns, `merge: Other make()` both,
# make evaluated once for each (docs/LMX_semantics.en.md#composition: operands are evaluated once, left to right).
# Before, the leading-atom reading gave the first no operand and dropped make() from the second.
# Exit 7; 81 if A's v is not Model's 1, 82 if B lost a field, 83 if make did not run exactly twice.
int: made 0
Model:
    int: v 1
end: Model
Other:
    int: w 2
end: Other
fn: make () Model
    node\made: node\made + 1
    return: Model
end: make
fn: count () int
    return: node\made
end: count
fn: m () int
    A: merge: make()
    if: A\v != 1
        return: 81
    B: merge: Other make()
    if: B\v * 10 + B\w != 12
        return: 82
    if: count() != 2
        return: 83
    return: 7
end: m
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: m(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
